rmula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\,125 & =\\frac{50}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(50-1)(\\frac{5}{7})) \\\\ 1\\,125 & =25(2{a}_{1}+35) \\\\ 45 & =2{a}_{1}+35 \\\\ 10 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346504 13194139535375 true] [17592186346503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346505 13194139535375 true] [17592186346503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346506 13194139535375 true] [17592186346503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346507 13194139535375 true] [17592186346503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346508 13194139535375 true] [17592186346503 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535375 true] [17592186346503 1041 "selection" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346503 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346508 13194139535375 true] [17592186346503 1110 #uuid "b24a8251-4adc-524e-a1bc-b29c7a641046" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346504 1034 "20" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346504 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346504 1111 #uuid "d10f67f3-e3a5-59b2-ac48-761a46619e20" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346505 1034 "10" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346505 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346505 1111 #uuid "924c4bce-ef7a-5f25-8774-6a91e18d2288" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346506 1034 "2" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346506 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346506 1111 #uuid "18ccd489-19d4-5c15-8bfc-e40de8e0f34f" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346507 1034 "1" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346507 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346507 1111 #uuid "ce0fdce3-8392-5967-9f81-f041a1c3c674" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346508 1034 "5" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346508 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346508 1111 #uuid "442ad632-b186-59d7-b03e-13516bdf5927" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346509 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346510 13194139535375 true] [17592186346509 1089 "q-17480" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346509 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535375 true] [17592186346509 1100 "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=5,$ and the sum of the first $11$ terms is ${S}_{11}=374?$" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346509 1113 #uuid "74c2185e-8f4b-5ec1-b26d-368b6ce0b6b6" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346509 1145 "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=11$, $d=5$, and ${S}_{N}=374$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}374 & =\\frac{11}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(11-1)(5)) \\\\ 748 & =11(2{a}_{1}+50) \\\\ 68 & =2{a}_{1}+50 \\\\ 18 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346511 13194139535375 true] [17592186346510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346512 13194139535375 true] [17592186346510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346513 13194139535375 true] [17592186346510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346514 13194139535375 true] [17592186346510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346515 13194139535375 true] [17592186346510 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535375 true] [17592186346510 1041 "selection" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346510 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346511 13194139535375 true] [17592186346510 1110 #uuid "48c5d79b-1025-5769-a4f1-03838806c462" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346511 1034 "9" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346511 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346511 1111 #uuid "a3c44e16-fb90-585c-80e4-8748ab9d8efe" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346512 1034 "10" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346512 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346512 1111 #uuid "08db99c0-1045-5c89-85af-1203ef77c327" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346513 1034 "8" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346513 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346513 1111 #uuid "7cec6fe3-0d31-558b-a09e-ff9911139b34" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346514 1034 "6" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346514 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346514 1111 #uuid "a5d36972-8ae9-532a-8595-d19ce778b6f6" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346515 1034 "5" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346515 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346515 1111 #uuid "be0a640c-56ea-52d6-a828-cfcad9b86f36" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346516 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346517 13194139535375 true] [17592186346516 1089 "q-250865" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346516 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535375 true] [17592186346516 1100 "If the $10$th term of an arithmetic series is $-\\frac{1}{5}$ and the sum of the first $21$ terms is $0,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." 13194139535375 true] [17592186346516 1113 #uuid "3e9bdeaa-b79d-5303-b727-c7dd990da898" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346516 1145 "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=21$ and ${S}_{N}=0$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{21}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(21-1)d) \\\\ 0 & =21(2{a}_{1}+20d) \\\\ 0 & =2{a}_{1}+20d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $10$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{10} & ={a}_{1}+(10-1)d \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+9d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} & \\,\\,\\,=\\,{a}_{1}+9d \\\\ \\,0 & \\,\\,\\,=\\,2{a}_{1}+20d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & =-2{a}_{1}-18d \\\\ 0 & =2{a}_{1}+20d \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =2d \\\\ d & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=\\frac{1}{5}$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+9d \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+9(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{9}{5} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346518 13194139535375 true] [17592186346517 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535375 true] [17592186346517 1041 "field-1" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346517 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346518 13194139535375 true] [17592186346517 1110 #uuid "9153e017-e2b8-5cb0-b46d-fb67ba33257f" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346518 1034 "-2" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346518 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346518 1111 #uuid "b8292cad-17b0-54fa-9fb3-b8b754f481b2" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346519 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346520 13194139535375 true] [17592186346519 1089 "q-76376" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346519 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535375 true] [17592186346519 1100 "Find the first term of an arithmetic series if its $17$th term is $33$ and the sum of the first $30$ terms is $1\\,080.$" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346519 1113 #uuid "07fef979-0133-5e51-8e0b-bfcd37c2daee" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346519 1145 "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=30$ and ${S}_{N}=1\\,080$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 1\\,080 & =\\frac{30}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(30-1)d) \\\\ 1\\,080 & =15(2{a}_{1}+29d) \\\\ \\frac{1\\,080}{15} & =2{a}_{1}+29d \\\\ 72 & =2{a}_{1}+29d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $17$th term of the arithmetic series  and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{17} & ={a}_{1}+(17-1)d \\\\ 33 & ={a}_{1}+16d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}33={a}_{1}+16d \\\\ 72=2{a}_{1}+29d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-66 & =-2{a}_{1}-32d \\\\ 72 & =2{a}_{1}+29d \\\\ 6 & =-3d \\\\ d & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}33 & ={a}_{1}+16(-2) \\\\ 33 & ={a}_{1}-32 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =65.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346521 13194139535375 true] [17592186346520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346522 13194139535375 true] [17592186346520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346523 13194139535375 true] [17592186346520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346524 13194139535375 true] [17592186346520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346525 13194139535375 true] [17592186346520 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535375 true] [17592186346520 1041 "selection" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346520 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346523 13194139535375 true] [17592186346520 1110 #uuid "6ccf9c26-3ec6-5184-bfa6-411f920bb63a" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346521 1034 "71" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346521 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346521 1111 #uuid "6c5127d7-7fda-5258-859b-e3cd33af069d" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346522 1034 "62" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535375 true] [17592186346522 1111 #uuid "f535f8e3-1dd7-563c-9b80-567e9ceb987f" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346523 1034 "65" 13194139535375 true] [17592186346523 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1319413953